
mouse-joystick-pcb stage 3, idle and powered down.
36 V on J201, plus motor, encoder and limit switch.
Send 's' for the whole sequence, or 'b' to gate manually.

commands
  ?  this menu
  s  run the whole stage 3 sequence

  gates, in order
  b  rail up, bus closed, TMC51X0 attached and configured
  c  set CHOPCONF.vsense and read it back
  w  witness the limit switch by hand: actuate it while
     this runs (works with the driver disabled)
  W  witness it with the motor: sweep onto the switch and
     off again (needs 'e', so run 'c' first)
  e  ENABLE the driver (refuses unless vsense reads back 1)
  E  disable the driver

  motion
  j  jog +1 step     J  jog +10 steps
  k  jog -1 step     K  jog -10 steps
  g  encoder check: jog out and back, compare X_ENC
  h  home against the limit switch (bounded)
  H  homing repeatability, 5 runs
  t  measure the switch's reporting delay, two velocities
  n  set run current scale
  o  flip the encoder counting sense
  m  flip the motor direction (GCONF.shaft)
  y  flip which end of travel the switch is on

  angle output, for the motor-coupling test
  A  park the DAC at midscale (a static DC level)
  Z  park the DAC at zero scale
  F  park the DAC at full scale
     Park it, then jog or home, and AC-couple a scope on the
     BNC. The setpoint is DC, so anything AC is coupling.
  L  LIVE: drive the output from the encoder at 1 kHz until
     a key is pressed. Needs 'h' first. Reports the
     ACHIEVED rate, not the requested one.

  reporting
  p  position, velocity, encoder, switch, driver status
  d  ramp generator: mode, target, and every ramp register
  i  IOIN
  v  +3.3V_SW rail state
  I  beacon the board serial on the InstrumentPort
     triggers (no 36 V, no bus, no motion)
  x  power down: driver off, bus open, HV_EN low
  B  reboot into BOOTSEL      R  reboot

  one jog step = 1280 usteps = 9.00 deg at the motor shaft


##### send 'b' at +4.0 s
[1] rail and bus
    [ ok ] +3.3V_SW up in 132 ms, peak 3.294 V, method: firmware staircase
    [ ok ] bus closed, ~{TMC_DRV_EN} still high

[2] TMC51X0 over SPI0, driver disabled
    IOIN.VERSION = 0x11  [ ok ] TMC5130A
    [ ok ] motion-controller mode
    GSTAT: reset=0 drv_err=0 uv_cp=0
      reset=1 is expected on the first read after a rail
      power-up. uv_cp=0 means the charge pump is happy,
      which needs VS genuinely up.
    [ ok ] converter, driver, controller, encoder configured
      clock 16 MHz external (X1201), 256 usteps/fullstep,
      SpreadCycle, StealthChop off, CoolStep off
      ENC_CONST = +12.8 usteps per quadrature count, decimal mode.
      X_ENC now reads in microsteps, comparable to XACTUAL.
      Its scale reset to ZERO, so this write is what makes
      the encoder count at all.
[4] angle-output DAC
    transport: SPI1, write-only
    [ ok ] GAIN 0x101, 3.3000 V full scale at the BNC
      Output is at zero scale, which measures 4.5 mV on
      this board -- a clamp, not an offset. Park it with
      'A' before looking for motor coupling.


##### send 'c' at +7.3 s
[3] current: CHOPCONF.vsense, set and read back
    CHOPCONF = 0x10030153
    vsense read back = 1  [ ok ]
    TOFF nonzero = yes
    IRUN  = 8  -> 0.211 A RMS per coil
    IHOLD = 2  -> 0.070 A RMS per coil
      IHOLD_IRUN is write-only on the TMC5130A, so those two
      are what firmware wrote, not what was read back.
      CHOPCONF is the readable half of the decision, and
      vsense is the bit that carries the 1.8x error.
    motor WO-208-13-01D, 0.6 A rated. Ceiling IRUN 17 = 0.421 A RMS
      That ceiling reads the vendor's 0.6 A as a sine peak,
      the conservative of the two possible readings. Measure
      coil current and case temperature before raising it.
    [ ok ] safe to enable the output stage


